1
00:00:04,134 --> 00:00:07,334
Good morning, Fujimoto!

2
00:00:07,574 --> 00:00:09,694
Good morning!

3
00:00:12,104 --> 00:00:14,044
You know it's very early.

4
00:00:14,214 --> 00:00:15,504
Yes!

5
00:00:15,914 --> 00:00:19,744
Morning after morning...
what are you here for today?

6
00:00:20,114 --> 00:00:22,384
Yes. I'm here to help, today, too.

7
00:00:22,784 --> 00:00:23,854
Huh?

8
00:00:23,854 --> 00:00:26,654
Fujimoto, I am going to help you.

9
00:00:27,354 --> 00:00:28,724
Oh, man... You know...

10
00:00:28,724 --> 00:00:29,854
Oh?

11
00:00:30,324 --> 00:00:31,654
Good morning, Kobato.

12
00:00:31,894 --> 00:00:32,954
Fujimoto.

13
00:00:33,064 --> 00:00:34,534
Oh, good morning.

14
00:00:35,164 --> 00:00:36,494
Are you helping today, too?

15
00:00:36,664 --> 00:00:37,864
Yes.

16
00:00:38,764 --> 00:00:41,364
Fujimoto, that must be a great help for you.

17
00:00:41,474 --> 00:00:45,664
Give me a break, please! Why should
I need any help from anyone?!

18
00:00:45,904 --> 00:00:48,814
Kobato, don't give in. We're counting on you.

19
00:00:49,444 --> 00:00:51,284
Because at this rate, the moment you
take your eye off of him,

20
00:00:51,284 --> 00:00:53,714
he'll go out and push himself too hard again.

21
00:00:53,714 --> 00:00:54,584
Wha...

22
00:00:54,584 --> 00:00:55,484
Yes!

23
00:01:01,724 --> 00:01:04,864
Kobato.

24
00:01:04,864 --> 00:01:07,694
Kobato.
What should I do?

25
00:01:07,694 --> 00:01:12,104
Kobato.
Even the most obvious of things

26
00:01:13,004 --> 00:01:16,304
Are always such a challenge

27
00:01:16,304 --> 00:01:19,074
I want to laugh when I'm happy

28
00:01:19,074 --> 00:01:23,374
And sing whenever I want

29
00:01:23,944 --> 00:01:26,384
Is all

30
00:01:27,684 --> 00:01:32,054
They say my dreams will come true someday

31
00:01:32,484 --> 00:01:35,754
But when will "someday" come?

32
00:01:35,754 --> 00:01:39,254
I can't wait forever

33
00:01:39,394 --> 00:01:45,164
On "1, 2, 3!" I'll spread open my arms

34
00:01:45,164 --> 00:01:50,374
And let the light gather around me

35
00:01:50,374 --> 00:01:53,204
Where is it?

36
00:01:53,204 --> 00:01:56,544
Please tell me what I can do

37
00:01:56,544 --> 00:01:59,384
I make the most of getting hurt

38
00:01:59,384 --> 00:02:02,284
And run with all my might

39
00:02:02,284 --> 00:02:06,254
Despite how many dozens of times I fall

40
00:02:06,254 --> 00:02:09,294
And start crying

41
00:02:09,294 --> 00:02:13,314
I surprise myself

42
00:02:13,794 --> 00:02:17,964
In how much I believe in tomorrow

43
00:02:30,514 --> 00:02:32,144
Every single day...

44
00:02:38,124 --> 00:02:39,454
I'll do it myself!

45
00:02:40,954 --> 00:02:42,114
Oh that's right.

46
00:02:42,324 --> 00:02:45,364
I found this, so I'll put it
up here for you, okay?

47
00:02:45,364 --> 00:02:47,694
H-Hey, what are you doing?

48
00:02:53,434 --> 00:02:55,424
What else would you like me to do?

49
00:02:57,274 --> 00:02:59,944
...Kobato's Wish.

50
00:02:59,944 --> 00:03:01,844
...Kobato's Wish.
Where are you headed to today?

51
00:03:01,844 --> 00:03:02,314
Where are you headed to today?

52
00:03:03,114 --> 00:03:06,644
Yesterday you went to the library and the day
before that, you went to the university.

53
00:03:07,554 --> 00:03:08,914
I'm going to work.

54
00:03:09,154 --> 00:03:11,814
I've been told that you have
the day off from work.

55
00:03:14,154 --> 00:03:16,194
I've told you time and again. If it's sympa...

56
00:03:16,194 --> 00:03:18,284
It's not sympathy or curiosity.

57
00:03:20,634 --> 00:03:22,464
I thought I told you that you're being a nuisance.

58
00:03:23,964 --> 00:03:27,064
Fujimoto, have you ever taken a walk?

59
00:03:27,434 --> 00:03:28,404
Huh?

60
00:03:29,374 --> 00:03:31,864
Walks are good. They're fun.

61
00:03:32,604 --> 00:03:34,134
The only one having fun...

62
00:03:34,674 --> 00:03:36,374
Fun for you, perhaps.

63
00:03:37,614 --> 00:03:38,704
Let's go.

64
00:03:38,814 --> 00:03:40,154
To where we can have fun.

65
00:03:40,154 --> 00:03:41,374
H-Hey!

66
00:03:43,524 --> 00:03:45,954
That's right. The two of them went out.

67
00:03:49,124 --> 00:03:50,184
You're right.

68
00:03:51,164 --> 00:03:54,654
They just need time, like anyone else.

69
00:03:55,734 --> 00:03:58,534
Just like the two of you did.

70
00:04:13,244 --> 00:04:14,734
What are you trying to do?

71
00:04:18,584 --> 00:04:19,744
What is it?!

72
00:04:19,884 --> 00:04:21,584
Right here, on your face.

73
00:04:21,894 --> 00:04:24,514
It's always scrunched up.

74
00:04:26,094 --> 00:04:29,494
So that's why I want you to have fun.

75
00:04:33,574 --> 00:04:36,864
Boats! Fujimoto, let's get on a boat!

76
00:04:37,874 --> 00:04:39,864
What? A boat? But...

77
00:04:41,144 --> 00:04:42,474
Hey!

78
00:04:47,114 --> 00:04:49,554
It costs money to ride.

79
00:05:00,394 --> 00:05:01,954
Hey, come on.

80
00:05:03,704 --> 00:05:05,194
Hey.

81
00:05:05,704 --> 00:05:06,794
You're going to crash.

82
00:05:13,274 --> 00:05:14,174
Let me do it.

83
00:05:14,174 --> 00:05:17,344
N-No, I can't let you. You're injured.

84
00:05:17,684 --> 00:05:20,474
Then we'll never get back,
no matter how long you try!

85
00:05:22,184 --> 00:05:23,984
No matter how long?

86
00:05:28,194 --> 00:05:31,624
Kobato is ready! I will row with all my might!

87
00:05:41,074 --> 00:05:43,104
Don't dip the oar in too deep.

88
00:05:43,104 --> 00:05:44,264
Right.

89
00:05:44,444 --> 00:05:45,704
Use your legs, too.

90
00:05:45,944 --> 00:05:46,944
Right.

91
00:05:46,944 --> 00:05:48,934
Ready, go.

92
00:05:49,544 --> 00:05:51,414
Wow, we're moving!

93
00:05:51,514 --> 00:05:53,144
This is amazing!

94
00:05:53,754 --> 00:05:55,414
So carefree...

95
00:05:58,324 --> 00:05:59,814
Fujimoto.

96
00:06:00,324 --> 00:06:01,394
Huh?

97
00:06:01,394 --> 00:06:04,084
You look a little better up here.

98
00:06:10,864 --> 00:06:12,424
What's the big idea?

99
00:06:12,764 --> 00:06:18,074
Um, I wanted Fujimoto to cheer up,
so I got some food for the fish...

100
00:06:18,074 --> 00:06:19,404
That's not what I'm talking about!

101
00:06:19,404 --> 00:06:21,844
Do you know what predicament you're in?!

102
00:06:22,244 --> 00:06:26,744
Yes. I made him spend money again.

103
00:06:26,744 --> 00:06:28,844
But he did get the change...

104
00:06:30,624 --> 00:06:34,924
I'm telling you, that's not it! How many times
have I told you! We don't have time!

105
00:06:35,494 --> 00:06:38,014
Yes! So I'll do my best!

106
00:06:41,894 --> 00:06:43,364
We'd better hurry back.

107
00:06:43,704 --> 00:06:46,664
Hey! I'm not finished talking with you! Hey!

108
00:06:50,944 --> 00:06:53,774
Hello fish, I got some food for you!

109
00:06:54,374 --> 00:06:55,814
Are you there?

110
00:06:57,044 --> 00:06:58,844
Fujimoto, would you like to try?

111
00:06:59,144 --> 00:07:00,614
Just leave me alone.

112
00:07:03,114 --> 00:07:05,584
I can't relax with you following
me around wherever I go.

113
00:07:10,994 --> 00:07:12,514
I understand.

114
00:07:21,734 --> 00:07:23,174
Come on, let's go, Kobato!

115
00:07:23,174 --> 00:07:25,834
We've got to get as many kompeito as we can!

116
00:07:25,904 --> 00:07:27,104
Hello.

117
00:07:29,344 --> 00:07:30,604
Good afternoon.

118
00:07:30,884 --> 00:07:33,004
Oh, it's just you, Kohaku.

119
00:07:33,784 --> 00:07:37,714
Are you taking a stroll? It's such a
beautiful day today, isn't it?

120
00:07:38,384 --> 00:07:41,414
Aww, what is this overly cheerful atmosphere?!

121
00:07:41,554 --> 00:07:42,884
Is there a problem?

122
00:07:43,054 --> 00:07:46,554
Kohaku! From one carefree to another,
you can lecture her!

123
00:07:46,824 --> 00:07:48,034
Lecture Kobato?

124
00:07:48,034 --> 00:07:54,094
That's right! She's forgotten about her wish
and is fooling around, absentmindedly.

125
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,094
I have not forgotten.

126
00:07:56,204 --> 00:07:57,364
Oh yeah?!

127
00:07:58,944 --> 00:08:02,034
My wish has already been decided.

128
00:08:05,184 --> 00:08:06,704
Well of course.

129
00:08:45,184 --> 00:08:47,124
What is it with Dobato?

130
00:08:47,794 --> 00:08:49,484
I mean, she's just a Dobato.

131
00:08:49,754 --> 00:08:52,094
Are you angry, Ioryogi-san?

132
00:08:52,324 --> 00:08:54,314
You bet I'm angry!

133
00:08:56,364 --> 00:09:00,304
I'm angry, but when she gives
me a look like that...

134
00:09:01,304 --> 00:09:03,934
Kobato has made her decision, hasn't she?

135
00:09:04,544 --> 00:09:06,064
She's a fool.

136
00:09:07,144 --> 00:09:09,834
Nothing happens without purpose.

137
00:09:10,644 --> 00:09:13,874
And therefore, there is not a single
thing that has no meaning.

138
00:09:14,854 --> 00:09:16,684
Is that only true in Tenkai?

139
00:09:18,084 --> 00:09:20,024
Or could you say the same for residents of Ikai?

140
00:09:21,224 --> 00:09:25,684
For every being. For everything.

141
00:09:27,234 --> 00:09:28,424
I see.

142
00:09:34,674 --> 00:09:36,064
Fujimoto!

143
00:09:38,544 --> 00:09:40,804
Oh good. I found you.

144
00:09:42,314 --> 00:09:43,504
Why?

145
00:09:43,984 --> 00:09:45,104
Huh?

146
00:09:45,484 --> 00:09:47,174
Why do you bother with me?

147
00:09:48,084 --> 00:09:49,884
Why? Well, I...

148
00:09:50,454 --> 00:09:52,084
Do you want me to thank you?

149
00:09:53,054 --> 00:09:54,684
Then you're barking up the wrong tree.

150
00:09:55,124 --> 00:09:57,114
Because I don't feel thankful.

151
00:09:57,864 --> 00:09:59,454
And I never will.

152
00:10:03,194 --> 00:10:05,694
Because you mean a lot to me.

153
00:10:08,374 --> 00:10:11,894
It's natural to worry about a
person who is important to you.

154
00:10:15,374 --> 00:10:19,074
Ms. Sayaka has your organ stored away.

155
00:10:20,414 --> 00:10:21,944
I don't care about it.

156
00:10:22,784 --> 00:10:26,224
It's something that you care
very much about, isn't it?

157
00:10:27,524 --> 00:10:29,684
You can go and play it again, any time you like.

158
00:10:33,824 --> 00:10:35,054
What now?

159
00:10:35,894 --> 00:10:39,394
I was just thinking how you and
Ioryogi-san are so much alike.

160
00:10:39,834 --> 00:10:42,064
Like the way you're always angry.

161
00:10:42,604 --> 00:10:45,764
Ioryogi? The doll you're always carrying around?

162
00:10:45,944 --> 00:10:47,064
Yes.

163
00:10:47,414 --> 00:10:51,244
But he's actually very nice.

164
00:10:53,314 --> 00:10:54,974
Guess I'd better get going.

165
00:10:55,554 --> 00:10:57,144
Right.

166
00:10:58,354 --> 00:10:59,514
Kohaku.

167
00:11:00,724 --> 00:11:02,854
You made your decision as well, didn't you?

168
00:11:04,124 --> 00:11:05,284
Are you happy?

169
00:11:07,534 --> 00:11:08,724
Yes.

170
00:11:10,904 --> 00:11:14,064
Oh, what are you doing about your laundry?

171
00:11:14,734 --> 00:11:19,334
It must be difficult hanging it out. I could...

172
00:11:48,404 --> 00:11:49,704
Fujimoto.

173
00:11:51,674 --> 00:11:53,144
What is it?

174
00:11:53,644 --> 00:11:55,944
I cannot be with you tomorrow.

175
00:11:57,114 --> 00:12:00,814
Well, thank goodness. Freedom at last.

176
00:12:01,754 --> 00:12:06,344
If that makes you happy, then I'm happy too.

177
00:12:34,054 --> 00:12:35,344
Take care.

178
00:12:35,954 --> 00:12:37,384
Thank you very much.

179
00:12:38,954 --> 00:12:42,354
Oh, is that right. That's very sudden, isn't it?

180
00:12:42,724 --> 00:12:44,314
Thank you for all that you've done for me.

181
00:12:44,564 --> 00:12:47,854
I would have liked to say goodbye
to Chiho and Chise, too.

182
00:12:48,664 --> 00:12:50,424
I know they'll miss you.

183
00:12:51,464 --> 00:12:52,764
Have you spoken with Sayaka?

184
00:12:53,204 --> 00:12:55,564
I'm planning to see her now.

185
00:12:56,504 --> 00:12:57,664
Oh.

186
00:13:00,074 --> 00:13:03,944
It's been a year now since you came here.

187
00:13:04,584 --> 00:13:11,454
Yes. Four seasons. Spring,
summer, fall and winter.

188
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:13,554
I had so much fun each and every season.

189
00:13:15,494 --> 00:13:18,084
When you settle down, please get in touch.

190
00:13:20,224 --> 00:13:22,494
Yes. When I settle down.

191
00:13:29,204 --> 00:13:32,644
My wish has already been decided.

192
00:13:36,714 --> 00:13:41,014
Hey Dobato! You do know what
that means, don't you?

193
00:13:42,314 --> 00:13:43,014
Yes.

194
00:13:43,014 --> 00:13:45,484
If you can't fill the bottle with kompeito, you...

195
00:13:48,994 --> 00:13:51,394
Do you not care about what happens to you?

196
00:13:56,194 --> 00:13:57,754
Are you a fool, or what?

197
00:13:58,604 --> 00:14:00,224
Am I a fool?

198
00:14:01,904 --> 00:14:03,204
You're an absolute fool.

199
00:14:04,344 --> 00:14:06,534
One hundred percent.

200
00:14:13,814 --> 00:14:16,614
Ioryogi-san, sorry to keep you waiting.

201
00:14:17,214 --> 00:14:19,014
Are you finished with your farewells?

202
00:14:19,484 --> 00:14:20,954
Yes.

203
00:14:24,424 --> 00:14:25,654
Shall we go, then?

204
00:14:25,764 --> 00:14:26,954
Yes.

205
00:14:41,944 --> 00:14:44,314
Man, he's not home yet.

206
00:14:46,584 --> 00:14:48,644
Oh well. Perhaps it's better this way.

207
00:14:54,954 --> 00:14:57,394
Look. The moon is bright.

208
00:14:58,324 --> 00:14:59,554
Yes.

209
00:15:01,834 --> 00:15:03,384
You know what, Kobato?

210
00:15:03,734 --> 00:15:05,924
What is it, Ioryogi-san?

211
00:15:07,064 --> 00:15:12,134
Isn't it hard to just be with someone,
without really doing anything?

212
00:15:12,874 --> 00:15:15,934
Hard? Why?

213
00:15:17,744 --> 00:15:24,414
Just being able to be with someone
is a really wonderful thing.

214
00:15:36,364 --> 00:15:37,524
What?!

215
00:15:37,704 --> 00:15:39,794
I presumed you already heard.

216
00:15:40,164 --> 00:15:41,194
No.

217
00:15:41,834 --> 00:15:45,294
Perhaps it was difficult for her
to break the news to you.

218
00:15:46,704 --> 00:15:48,644
Did she tell you where she was going?

219
00:15:49,014 --> 00:15:52,604
No, just that she would be in
touch when she settled down.

220
00:15:55,054 --> 00:15:56,484
There he goes.

221
00:16:15,574 --> 00:16:17,034
He's here.

222
00:16:37,594 --> 00:16:39,064
Wait a minute!

223
00:16:39,224 --> 00:16:41,494
Please, wait! She really did her best!

224
00:16:41,634 --> 00:16:43,694
Yes, she's a bit foolish and
clumsy and an airhead,

225
00:16:43,694 --> 00:16:46,364
and all she has going for her is
her cheerfulness and honesty!

226
00:16:46,734 --> 00:16:48,674
But she's among the best humans
you will ever come across!

227
00:16:48,674 --> 00:16:50,834
She's got an incredible soul!

228
00:16:51,344 --> 00:16:54,104
So I beg you! Please don't eliminate her...

229
00:16:56,374 --> 00:16:58,344
Don't make her... disappear...

230
00:17:00,444 --> 00:17:04,444
Ioryogi-san, you're troubling Ushagi-san.

231
00:17:13,624 --> 00:17:15,254
I'm sorry, Kobato.

232
00:17:16,294 --> 00:17:20,564
Please don't apologize. This is my decision.

233
00:17:22,504 --> 00:17:23,934
I...

234
00:17:24,974 --> 00:17:27,734
Thank you very much, Ioryogi-san.

235
00:17:46,924 --> 00:17:48,524
What are you doing?!

236
00:17:49,264 --> 00:17:50,824
Fujimoto?

237
00:17:55,434 --> 00:17:57,134
Where do you think you're going?

238
00:17:58,474 --> 00:18:00,304
I don't know.

239
00:18:00,304 --> 00:18:01,864
Is this supposed to be a joke?!

240
00:18:02,374 --> 00:18:04,714
You're scolding me right to the last moment.

241
00:18:04,884 --> 00:18:09,044
What do you expect?! What's the big idea
disappearing without a word to me?!

242
00:18:09,254 --> 00:18:10,844
I'm sorry.

243
00:18:12,654 --> 00:18:15,094
Was it something I said?

244
00:18:15,094 --> 00:18:17,524
No! Not at all!

245
00:18:17,694 --> 00:18:19,094
Then, why?!

246
00:18:22,194 --> 00:18:23,994
It's in her contract.

247
00:18:24,604 --> 00:18:25,604
Who said that?!

248
00:18:25,604 --> 00:18:28,504
Over here. On top of the baggage.

249
00:18:30,704 --> 00:18:32,074
Hi.

250
00:18:33,874 --> 00:18:35,504
This is Ioryogi-san.

251
00:18:36,314 --> 00:18:38,874
But... he's a... doll...

252
00:18:39,314 --> 00:18:41,504
I was just pretending to be.

253
00:18:44,724 --> 00:18:46,584
We're talking about the contract, right?

254
00:18:47,724 --> 00:18:49,454
Kobato, show him.

255
00:18:52,164 --> 00:18:53,184
Yes sir.

256
00:18:54,024 --> 00:18:55,034
W-Wait.

257
00:18:55,034 --> 00:18:56,294
What's this about?

258
00:19:00,134 --> 00:19:03,124
What the... what is that?

259
00:19:04,674 --> 00:19:06,304
She's dead.

260
00:19:07,504 --> 00:19:11,964
Kobato's present soul does not
belong in any of our worlds.

261
00:19:12,544 --> 00:19:15,144
It's not a life, just a peaceful existence.

262
00:19:16,254 --> 00:19:18,984
But thanks to a contract with
a particular big shot,

263
00:19:19,484 --> 00:19:23,924
she was given one and only one chance to
be reborn and live life all over again.

264
00:19:23,924 --> 00:19:26,364
Wait a minute! What in the world
are you talking about?!

265
00:19:26,564 --> 00:19:27,794
However...

266
00:19:29,534 --> 00:19:35,124
Kobato chose to spend her remaining time with
you, rather than fulfill the terms of her contract.

267
00:19:35,734 --> 00:19:38,934
And therefore, the contract... was nullified.

268
00:19:45,284 --> 00:19:49,474
And that's why I must disappear.

269
00:19:51,684 --> 00:19:53,124
You're lying! Hey!

270
00:19:54,054 --> 00:19:58,954
Fujimoto, being with you made me very happy.

271
00:20:03,364 --> 00:20:04,854
I can't do it.

272
00:20:06,064 --> 00:20:09,034
I was hoping to stay smiling at the end.

273
00:20:15,544 --> 00:20:18,804
No! Don't do this! I beg you!

274
00:20:21,014 --> 00:20:22,504
Fujimoto.

275
00:20:24,454 --> 00:20:26,544
You are very precious to me.

276
00:20:28,494 --> 00:20:29,824
You have been...

277
00:20:31,324 --> 00:20:32,524
And you will continue to be.

278
00:20:33,864 --> 00:20:34,984
Forever.

279
00:20:36,794 --> 00:20:38,164
Don't go.

280
00:21:03,294 --> 00:21:04,954
Kompeito?

281
00:21:11,134 --> 00:21:12,364
What's this?

282
00:21:15,234 --> 00:21:17,004
The kompeito...

283
00:21:18,574 --> 00:21:20,064
The bottle is filling up.

284
00:21:25,984 --> 00:21:29,144
Kobato's wish has changed.

285
00:21:30,654 --> 00:21:33,344
But the contract cannot be changed.

286
00:21:34,954 --> 00:21:37,324
About going to the place she wants to go.

287
00:21:38,664 --> 00:21:42,564
Fujimoto's... Kompeito...

288
00:21:43,594 --> 00:21:44,894
So warm.

289
00:21:45,364 --> 00:21:49,274
This is more like a curse! Please!

290
00:21:49,274 --> 00:21:52,174
Please let Kobato live in this world!

291
00:22:01,454 --> 00:22:02,714
Darn...

292
00:22:03,054 --> 00:22:05,784
I'm sorry I couldn't be of more help.

293
00:22:06,854 --> 00:22:09,654
Don't apologize. I feel the same way.

294
00:22:10,354 --> 00:22:12,554
I was with her the longest.

295
00:22:13,894 --> 00:22:15,594
And yet I can't do anything.

296
00:22:16,994 --> 00:22:21,124
But if there is a purpose to all that happens...

297
00:22:23,004 --> 00:22:24,834
What is going on?

298
00:22:25,804 --> 00:22:29,294
I have to go where I ought to go.

299
00:22:31,784 --> 00:22:33,404
Goodbye.

300
00:22:35,014 --> 00:22:35,984
Wait.

301
00:23:01,944 --> 00:23:05,904
Nakushita mono to

302
00:23:07,884 --> 00:23:12,714
Atsumeta mono no hazama ni

303
00:23:13,724 --> 00:23:20,824
Anata no egao ochiteita no

304
00:23:21,434 --> 00:23:26,864
Todokisou de todokanai

305
00:23:28,034 --> 00:23:32,594
Tonde yukeru wake janai shi

306
00:23:33,944 --> 00:23:39,014
Warawasete agetai dake na no ni,

307
00:23:39,014 --> 00:23:44,384
Yaku tatazu no kono tsubasa

308
00:23:44,924 --> 00:23:50,154
Nan no tame ni aru no darou?

309
00:23:51,024 --> 00:23:56,364
Anata no soba de warau yo,

310
00:23:56,694 --> 00:24:01,224
Watashi ni dekiru koto

311
00:24:02,734 --> 00:24:08,234
Atatameru dake de mo ii no kana

312
00:24:08,344 --> 00:24:12,784
Semete tsutsumitai

313
00:24:13,544 --> 00:24:20,154
Kizuku no, sono tame no tsubasa to

314
00:24:20,154 --> 00:24:26,124
Ima koso watashi warau yo

315
00:24:26,124 --> 00:24:28,534
Next episode
The Day to Come...
Ima koso watashi warau yo

316
00:24:28,534 --> 00:24:30,764
Next episode
The Day to Come...

